{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYzCnMA1L8ibS8EXaLo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Granary v2, the dataset pipeline behind NVIDIA's Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe, gives every recording three transcript versions. For the utterance \"I paid, uh, twenty-five euros,\" the targets are the spoken form with disfluencies as words, a written form with disfluencies (\"I paid, uh, €25.\"), and a clean written form (\"I paid €25.\"). These are labeled tn_raw, itn_raw and itn_clean in the public manifests. NVIDIA says a promptable speech model needs training data with unambiguous formatting targets, and these are the same verbatim and clean styles a developer can request from Transcribe in a prompt.\n\nThe public manifest covers 463,062 hours across 48 languages and 16 source corpora, up from 25 languages in Granary v1. NVIDIA notes that these figures describe the dataset release, not Transcribe's full training mixture or its sampling weights. The manifests also carry task labels, entity hints, provenance and a per-record quality flag. Audio is not bundled, so users download it from each source corpus under its original license.\n\nThe curation steps are where the quality control sits. In the transcription stage, each language is routed to a primary and a recovery ASR model, and the recovery model takes over when the primary fails a hallucination check. Human reference transcripts, where available, help keep trusted spellings. The next stage checks character rate, hallucination patterns and agreement with the model or human reference, and only records that pass receive contextual-ASR terms and translations. A separate high-fidelity stage removes noisy, clipped or multi-speaker segments, which cut VoxPopuli from 354k hours to 111k hours across 22 European languages.\n\nNVIDIA's medical ASR case study applies the same idea to fine-tuning, with instructions that specify the required convention for digits, unit spacing and brand-name hyphens. Developers can run the NeMo Curator pipeline on their own recordings or authorized public corpora, so the pipeline can be reused to build targets for a specialized domain."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2010,"cache_read_input_tokens":6676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2010},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36151e93-a157-48a1-8c2d-a29815113b4f","uuid":"5944b7ce-3d4a-4c3e-9356-c431297d9ca9","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:30:51.900Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYzCaT8M8MM5Evo5giF"}
